   "produced_at": "2026-11-02T14:05:55+00:00",
   "agent_notes": [
    "Ancient tradition (Targum Ps-Jonathan on 20:16) reads that Abimelech was kept from Sarah that very night; a longer interval would conflict with 20:4 'had not drawn near'. Treated as one night. Not split into three beats since the dream is a single continuous speech exchange."
   ],
   "history": [
    {
     "status": "approved",
     "at": "2026-11-02T14:07:38+00:00",
     "note": "[consider] If revised: cite Targum Pseudo-Jonathan on 20:16 in the temporal_reasoning_note as the basis for the first night, rather than 20:4, or widen the margin to a few days. (GEN.20.18: \"For the LORD had fast closed up all the wombs of the house of Abimelech\"; Targum Ps.-Jonathan on GEN.20.16: \"one night\" (לילא חדא))",
     "by": "urim-critic@3 · claude-opus-5-5"
    }
   ],
   "source": null
  }
